A||||4||Urchin||Insurance question||||1||
Z||000000||Urchin||05-22-2001||09:03 PM||||My fiero is not on the road right now.  I have another car for an everyday driver and I want to put my fiero back on the road for weekends, cruises, etc.  So my question is, does anyone know of an insurance company that will insure you for weekends only, or maybe a limited amount of driving?  I've called a couple, and the ones I have called don't offer anything of the sort.  I don't know if such a policy exists, but I thought maybe someone on here would know for sure.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_8.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||05-22-2001||09:20 PM||||My insurance policy for the Fieros is for parades, car shows, club events, repairs. Its alimited use policy with an insured appraised value on the car.<P>So I drove to Daytona, NIFE get together in Illinois, Carlisle show, next week to the Dells, a couple of weeks later to Maine, later in July back to Illinois to pick up my car after some painting in Illinois, then Williamsburg FOCOA event.<P>Some risk if you use the car for other than stated purposes.<P>Lots of driving, not much locally.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Oreif||05-22-2001||10:19 PM||||You can insure it as a "pleasure" vehicle or you can insure it as a "collectable" or "showcar". The collectable/showcar usually require an appraisal. Pleasure cars are insured as not daily driven. You can check with your insurance company and see how they handle the different classes of cars. You can also check with local car clubs. Antique status is very restrictive and requires special plates. Mine is insured as a collectable and is insured for it's appraised value. (as an added benefit I'm exempt from emission testing!)<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierofreek2001||05-22-2001||10:38 PM||||good luck with the "classic car"/ "show car" insurance, most companies are very strict with their guidelines on what they can insure and cant, ... i work at GEICO, and i decline way more people then i accept because of all the rules<BR>steve||||reg||1
Z||000004||Urchin||05-22-2001||10:59 PM||||Hmmmm.   Well thanks for the help guys.  I guess I'll make some more calls and see what happens.  My insurance company for my Z24 did not offer any type of limited coverage, so looks like I'll be going elsewhere for the fiero.  But, if you guys have that type of coverage, it's obviously out there.  I just haven't found it yet.  <BR>Thanks.<BR><P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_8.jpg"> ||||reg||1
